# Release-critical paths. Any change here needs Randy's review, which is what
# stops a contributor from altering the publish path, the package identity, or
# the scanners that gate a release.
#
# This only takes effect once the main ruleset has "Require review from Code
# Owners" enabled.
#
# Deliberately no catch-all `*` owner: with require_code_owner_review on, a
# catch-all makes every PR need the owner's approval and leaves the owner's own
# PRs unsatisfiable, since an author cannot be their own code-owner reviewer.
# Ordinary code changes therefore need any one approval; only the release path
# needs the owner specifically.

/.github/workflows/ @randiskull
/.github/dependabot.yml @randiskull
/package.json @randiskull
/package-lock.json @randiskull
# Pins the published surface: the entry point resolves, and `files` stays
# an allowlist rather than a denylist with hand-maintained negations.
/test/package-constraints.test.ts @randiskull
/scripts/ @randiskull
/CODEOWNERS @randiskull
